our goal here was to create what we  believe is the first RPG where the mage  is a total badass okay and one of the  ways that we started approaching this is  we looked at what a lot of games have  implemented and the sort of constraints  they place on mages to make them equal  to other classes that they put in the  game and we eliminated them so we took  away things like Nana bars and cool  downs and what's really interesting  about that is when we tell people that  they usually come back and say well  doesn't that in the mean the game is  going to be trivial because you can just  cast as much magic as you want to write  you're not limited the game is actually  very very challenging and I think Josh  will give you an idea of how challenging  it can be yeah so as the producer on the  game obviously I play it quite a bit and  I practice the four packs to get ready  and I came in feeling kind of confident  and I said to myself that I didn't want  to die a single time at PAX we're doing  about 60 demos for crowds of 20 folks  and I felt like I'd be embarrassed if I  ever died once and then on Friday over  the course of the day I died 24 times so  that gives you some sense of this is not  an easy game by any stretch it's not  impossible it's a lot of fun but it's  definitely a challenge and you need to  learn the skills to play it properly so  another thing that we did is you know we  took a look at how we've been  conditioned to play mages in  over the years and we have terms like  glass cannon and squishy right which  mean I can deal out a lot of damage but  I can never stand toe-to-toe with an  enemy I need to run away from them i  need to kite things like that and we  wanted to eliminate that so we decided  to focus on a couple of defensive  abilities and we weaponize them so your  block as an example which is on the  right mouse button when you block you  ignore half of all damage however if you  time your block perfectly then you're  not only invulnerable to all damage for  that brief window but if you're hit by  an enemy like like this you will  detonate whatever spell that you haven't  wet so when you can actually turn your  defensive block into an offensive weapon  and it's really visceral feeling then  the other defensive ability is your  magical dodge or a blink and when you do  that you have a short teleport and  wherever you land your again going to  detonate whatever spell you have a quit  so now instead of running away from your  enemies constantly you can dodge into  your enemies and then block them and  just really fight toe-to-toe and it's  it's very very visible we've got some  pretty awesome voice talent in the game  our female hero is voiced by jennifer  hale and Troy Baker does the male hero  and we've also got Gina Torres and  Clancy Brown doing voice work for us so  really incredible cast of characters in  the game this area right here is  something kind of neat we call these  loot machines right now and these are  challenges that are sprinkled all  through the game and they all work  differently this particular one when you  hit it with a spell it starts an event  that starts spawning waves of enemies in  this case for our waves and every time  you kill an enemy if they drop loot  you'll notice the loot doesn't actually  go to the player they  goes up into the machine instead and as  more loot is added in the machine the  loot that's in there will promote to a  better and better quality and you can  get to the point where like in this case  right now there's a legendary in there  however you can't get any of that loop  unless you beat the entire encounter and  if you die at any point you lose all the  loot that's there and you got to come  back and try it again these are optional  areas are designed to be very  challenging but very rewarding at the  cleric and accomplished as you can see  josh is on his last leg here he's got  his last shield pip up he took a lot of  damage because this mini boss right here  in the last wave she's a banshee she  does a scream that will stun you and she  stuns you right in the middle of enemies  he could go pretty poorly right when  she's by herself when you get to the end  she's not so bad  that's correct there's no madam nope  yeah there's no man oh there's no you  know there's we have a couple of systems  like your blink is something you can't  spam it you can just use it over and  over again but they're in there are no  cool downs or anything that interrupts a  player for more than two or three  seconds so now that josh has completed  that room he's got a ton of loot right  from that glute machine so he's going to  go ahead and craft a little bit explain  how that works so I'm about to make my  way into a boss battle here and for that  I'm going to need some better spells all  the loot in the game is focused on being  able to craft yourself new magical  spells and so for a quick demonstration  I'm gonna grab some new fire spells to  fight the boss with so I choose my fire  sigil and my strategy is going to be to  apply a debuff to him using a mastery  focus spell so I'm building a targeted  spell and I'm going to augment it with  mastery and when I crap that and equip  it that goes into my arsenal then I'm  going to craft a barrier spell and I'm  going to use that for damage I've got a  lot of choices here I like this one and  I'm going to add destruction to this so  the basic idea is light them on fire and  get them burning with this mastery  debuff I then follow up with my barrier  spell which I can cast by either  blinking or blocking and that's going to  do bonus damage against them fun in here  i'll do an AoE as well just to round out  the Arsenal and more destruction because  destruction helps so now I've equipped  all my new spells I've got my old spell  sitting in my inventory and they're not  useful to me anymore so I'm going to go  into our synthesis screen where you can  synthesize any of the lewd or spells in  the game